Here is the commit message:
HADOOP-12407. Test failing: hadoop.ipc.TestSaslRPC. (stevel)

Here is the root cause:
The bug was caused by the test method `testSaslPlainServerBadPassword()` expecting an exact error message when a wrong password was provided during SASL authentication. This approach was too rigid, as it did not account for variations in the error message format, leading to test failures when the actual message did not match the expected string exactly.

Here is the patch:

   @Test
   public void testSaslPlainServerBadPassword() {
     SaslException e = null;
     try {
       runNegotiation(
           new TestPlainCallbacks.Client("user", "pass1"),
           new TestPlainCallbacks.Server("user", "pass2"));
     } catch (SaslException se) {
       e = se;
     }
     assertNotNull(e);
-    assertEquals("PLAIN auth failed: wrong password", e.getMessage());
+    String message = e.getMessage();
+    assertContains("PLAIN auth failed", message);
+    assertContains("wrong password", message);
   }

